    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text>{@ta1@},{@ta2@},x = {@x@}, y = {@y@}</text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>This question is based on the theorem that opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral add up to 180° in the section Angles in a Cyclic Quadrilateral of the CBC Grade 11 Mathematics textbook (INNODEMS). The angles are never 90° and never equal or supplementary to each other, so the wrong-pair and equal-angles mistakes can be told apart.</p>
<p id="concept">Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral</p>]]></text>
    </questiondescription>
